{
  "summary": "Adds btck_chainstate_manager_options_set_prune_target() and related constants to the libbitcoinkernel C API and C++ wrapper. This allows kernel callers to configure automatic, manual, or disabled block pruning on btck_ChainstateManagerOptions. It also validates prune target boundaries and includes unit tests for pruned chainstate manager construction.",
  "problem": "libbitcoinkernel provides no way to configure block pruning on ChainstateManagerOptions. Any attempt to use libbitcoinkernel with an existing pruned data directory fails during LoadChainstate() because the block manager detects prior pruning while chainstate load options default to unpruned mode, forcing an abort.",
  "evidence": [
    "Fixes #35627 ('kernel: can't work with pruned blocksdir')",
    "Author notes datadir loading fails with: '[error] Failed to load chain state from your data directory: You need to rebuild the database using -reindex to go back to unpruned mode.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
