  },
  "scope_notes": "The diff was not provided in the prompt, but metadata shows a small addition (+65/-0) across kernel API headers, implementation, C++ wrapper, and kernel unit tests.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Libbitcoinkernel callers cannot currently configure block pruning, which causes attempts to open existing pruned data directories to fail during chainstate load. This PR exposes btck_chainstate_manager_options_set_prune_target and manual/minimum pruning constants in the C API and C++ wrapper with boundary validation. It resolves issue #35627, allowing libbitcoinkernel consumers to load and run against pruned data directories.",
